  "scope": {
    "summary": "A 100 ms timer between two service tasks — the scheduler's claim path under load.",
    "measures": [
      "arming a timer row from database time (clock_timestamp() + interval) and the NOTIFY that wakes sleeping schedulers",
      "the scheduler's claim: pick the due candidate off the due_at index without a lock, take the instance row lock, re-check, fire and delete the row in one transaction",
      "how far past due_at a timer actually fires when many are due at once — that gap is the p50 latency minus the 100 ms floor"
    ],
    "excludes": [
      "long waits: a sleeping timer is a passive row and costs nothing, which is precisely why the model uses 100 ms rather than a realistic deadline",
      "timer cycles, which this engine does not support",
      "history levels: every event is written"
    ],
